WEBVTT

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.340
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.300
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.600
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.950
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:27.190
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:30.860
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:41.570
I want this voice to reach you, even though it’s still a tiny song.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:47.740
That’s because I have the feeling that something’s gonna start.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:01:02.840
As I was cowering, muffling my voice, the tears that I shed

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:11.430
probably helped me notice that

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:17.340
I’ve almost forgotten how to believe.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:26.200
The future that I painted (I will fulfill it)

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.570
Looking up to the clear skies,

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:38.710
I begin to run once again. Someday, I want to dye

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:44.500
that white sky with my colors.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:51.510
I’m going to fly as far as possible, shining like a marble,

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.890
unfolding these wings of mine.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.090
Kanmuri’s secret!!

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.270
A jam showdown without moral codes!

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.300
Looks delicious!

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.480
Mama, this one too!

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.190
Is this it?

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:22.810
Yes sir!

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.270
Let’s go.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:24.750
Yes sir!

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:38.880
The Austrian Court Chef
Remarkable!! Tsutsumi Masanobu, the first Japanese to ever pass!

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:40.960
Impressive as always...

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:43.140
Kanmuri, what are you doing?

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.460
Kawachi-san!

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.090
What, you looking at porn?

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.300
Let me see too!

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.090
Hey!

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:49.840
Huh?

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:50.650
What is this?

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:51.220
The Austrian Court Chef
Remarkable!! Tsutsumi Masanobu, the first Japanese to ever pass!

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.150
The Austrian court chef, Tsutsumi Masanobu.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.030
It’s that superb chef who is the first Japanese
person to have been eligible for the post, fight?

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.990
I heard that it’s a really hard qualification that you can apply for only once in all your life.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.620
Do you plan on giving up being a
baker and aiming for this instead?

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.830
Are you trying to escape from the battle against St. Pierre?!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:11.370
Of course not!

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.710
Then, what is it?

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.170
Uh, th-that is...

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.300
W-We’ve got trouble!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:19.760
The Manager is fighting these scary guys outside!

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.260
Having you guys hanging around outside our store is...

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.650
troublesome for our other customers!

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:36.610
He’s strong.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:37.480
He’s really strong!

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.530
He’s not human!

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.740
Who the hell are you?

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.240
A mere baker.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.200
Liar!

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.110
Get him.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:48.120
Do you understand what taking that out means?

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.910
Huh? It means that you’re gonna die, of course.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.830
Not quite.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:55.830
It means that if you’re unable to take me down in one go, <i>you’re</i> gonna die.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.550
M-Master Shigeru!

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.640
Master Shigeru?

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.550
Let’s stop with this kind of thing, shall we?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:07.810
Our...

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.810
Our deepest apologies!

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.060
What the...?

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.230
Why is everyone bowing to Kanmuri?

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.270
Wasn’t Bocchan by Natsume Souseki?

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.320
Well, it’s not too hard to guess what they’re here for...

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:20.820
Kanmuri...

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.150
Who the hell...?

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:22.900
Are you...?

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:26.320
What was that?!

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.370
Your father is...?!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.830
The head of the biggest yakuza group in Japan, the Hashiguchi family?!

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.710
Sorry about that.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.080
First I’ve heard of this.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.380
I’m really surprised.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:38.920
Yeah.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:44.970
Initially, my mother was the daughter of a rich family that had nothing to do with the yakuza.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.050
She was attracted to the
wild nature of my young father

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.720
and married him despite the objections of those around her.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.930
But in the end, due to
discord between their personalities...

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.350
They got divorced?

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.310
Yes.

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.480
That is why I bear my mother’s maiden name.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.780
So, what is it that they want from you after all this time?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.240
That’s simple enough.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:05.320
They want me to join the yakuza.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:05.570
What?!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.530
What was that?!
What?!

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.540
My father has another son with yet another name.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:16.380
He came to us saying that he wants one of us to carry on after him.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:18.630
You have a sibling, Kanmuri?

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:19.920
Yeah.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.960
It seems that he’s called Tsutsumi Masanobu.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.720
I seem to have heard the name somewhere...

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.220
Isn’t that him...?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:29.220
The court chef we were reading about on the net?

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.680
Yeah, that’s right.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.140
So, what are you going to do?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.810
Are you really going to be the head of the yakuza?

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.810
Of course not!

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.060
While it may bring me money and power, I really don’t want to become a thug.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:42.820
In that case, that Tsutsumi guy can inherit, right?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.690
Nope, it’s not that easy.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.990
Because Tsutsumi-san feels the same way I do about this.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:51.950
If there’s nobody to inherit, then what happens?

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:55.910
Well... that won’t quite work out either...

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.590
But to think that you have to battle with this
Tsutsumi guy on the next Yakitate!! 9 show...

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:08.630
And that the person who loses
must give up on his dream

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.890
and inherit the position of the
fourth-generation head of the group...

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.930
That’s really cruel.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.020
Why did you accept these conditions?

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:18.770
I’m up against the biggest yakuza group in Japan.

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:23.320
If I go up against them, we can be sure that Pantasia
would have to face terrible harassment as well.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:26.280
But, if you lose...

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.030
I’ll quit Pantasia.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.580
I’ll have no choice but to give up and inherit.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.160
Don’t worry...

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.000
All I have to do is win.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.750
After all, if it comes down to bread,
my skills should be superior to his.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.420
Don’t worry, Kanmuri!

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.550
You can’t expect much of
Kawachi, but I’m here with you!

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:50.550
I’ll be sure to keep you from becoming a yakuza!

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.550
A... Azuma-kun...

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:53.970
That’s right, Kanmuri.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.890
You can’t expect much of me, but Azuma is there.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:56.810
Geez.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.430
What are you making me say, you idiot?

00:06:58.850 --> 00:06:59.730
Listen up.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:01.730
However great a chef the opponent is,

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:03.560
that’s in Austria.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:07.440
The ingredients used in Europe and the ingredients
used in Japan are completely different.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:12.950
The rule of this show is that you’re supposed to
use the specialty ingredients of the city chosen.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.450
So, we should have a great advantage on him.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.450
Once in a while, you actually say something good.

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:22.670
Right? It’s a shame though that it’s
only once in a while I say something good.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.750
You made me say something again!

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.800
Why must <i>I</i> get hit?

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.470
Well anyway, let’s not give up
and keep our chins up.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:31.970
You’re right.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.230
Well then, we will now
select the city for the fifth match.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.140
What panel would the St. Pierre
representative like to pick?

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.690
Nine, please.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.190
All right, let’s see what’s below panel nine.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.440
Shinanomachi

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.730
Shi... Shinanomachi?

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:49.940
The worst possible choice.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:50.240
Shinanomachi

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.200
Shinanomachi refers to the city of Shinanomachi
in the Kamiminochi district of Nagano prefecture.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.530
May I ask something, Kuro-yan?
Shinanomachi

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.790
Personal comments are not permitted.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.040
How many times must I tell you that?

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.790
You want to lose your hair that badly?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:05.580
But... red letters mean that the topic’s
been decided beforehand again, right?

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:06.960
Please tell us quickly.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.420
Always in such a bloody hurry...

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:08.710
Shinanomachi

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:09.920
Let’s flip the panel once again!
Shinanomachi

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:10.630
Jam

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.720
Last time it was green onion bread...

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.890
This time we must make jam buns, huh?

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.220
No!

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:18.470
You don’t need to make the bread.

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:19.640
You just have to make the jam.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:20.520
And that’s how it is.

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:22.390
Huh? Why?!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:23.890
It is the requirement of the show’s committee.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.900
Just making bread would lead
to a loss of interest in the show.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:27.730
It can’t be...

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.690
This time, you must make it from the specialty products of Shinanomachi.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:32.900
We are looking forward to a truly high quality jam.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:33.740
That’s all.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.620
Th... The worst possibility of all possibilities.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:42.080
Let’s disassemble quickly, shall we?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:42.660
Yep.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.460
Studios get really cold once the lights are switched off...

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.670
Yeah...

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.840
What’s wrong, Kanmuri...?

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:52.840
You’re cold too?

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.840
The Sachertorte cake and the Berliner bun...

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:01.640
Two Austrian food items
considered famous all over the world...

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:03.020
Do you guys know anything about them?

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.350
You know anything, Kawachi?

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.350
Of course not.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:06.560
Jam.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:07.350
They both have jam!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:08.860
Jam?

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:15.780
The Tyrol region in Austria is world famous for
having the longest-known history of jam-making.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:20.870
So famous, that they have jam-making tours for tourists who come to visit.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:24.870
They say that in France, even elementary school kids can make bread.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:28.380
But in Austria, they say even kindergarteners can make jam.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.900
In other words,

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:34.970
we’re going to have to fight the opponent at the topic that he’s most skilled at.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:37.890
Exactly.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.390
Your knowledge is just as extensive as the rumors say.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:43.140
Pleased to meet you,
Kanmuri Shigeru-kun.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.650
I heard that you’re a genius who
graduated from Harvard at age 16?

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.150
I’m proud to have a little brother like you.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.980
Ts... Tsutsumi-san...

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:55.400
In that case, you should be able to recognize this taste.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.660
Th-This is...

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:00.910
The Austrian jam doughnut, a Berliner!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.370
It looks like our fried bread...

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.410
Let me taste it.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.300
Wh-What is this?!

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:20.140
M-My body is...

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:27.100
Ballerina!

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:31.810
F-Fearsome...

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:32.230
Tsutsumi-san’s Berliner is forcing him to become a ballerina.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.480
Un, deux, trois.
Tsutsumi-san’s Berliner is forcing him to become a ballerina.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:36.280
Th... This is the legendary taste that is
acknowledged by the Austrian royalty, huh?

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.780
Ballerina
Th... This is the legendary taste that is
acknowledged by the Austrian royalty, huh?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:40.740
Berliner
Ballerina
Th... This is the legendary taste that is
acknowledged by the Austrian royalty, huh?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:45.370
Real jam can only be made by someone who has studied Austrian culture.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.870
Anything other than that is mere fruit concentrate.

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:56.880
Is this seat taken?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:57.670
Go ahead.

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.720
Could you be... Tsutsumi-san?!

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:01.890
That’s right.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.300
Amazing!

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:06.020
You’re the Austrian court chef even though you’re Japanese.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:10.190
You’re the star of hope for old men without any special talent like us.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.730
Am I all that famous?

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:14.690
I have a kid, but...

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.690
he’s no good at his studies.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.490
I’d like for him to grow into a great man like you, but...

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:23.030
Even I was a complete idiot
when I was a child, you know...

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:24.070
How surprising...

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:26.580
I’d thought that you were
a genius from birth.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:31.460
Huh? Did I say something to upset you?

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:37.090
You see, I have this really smart
younger brother born of a different mother.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:40.260
I really, really hated being compared to him.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.590
Which is why I desperately looked for
something I was good at and worked hard at it.

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.100
Oh? Is that so?

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:50.680
I don’t think that human beings can become strong simply by living happy, blessed lives.

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:53.190
If you really want to raise your son to be like me...

00:11:54.400 --> 00:12:00.190
you must occasionally condition him to have
a strong inferiority complex and a deep hatred.

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:00.780
Shinanomachi

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:03.240
Oh, this is Shinanomachi, huh?
Shinanomachi

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:04.950
It has a really beautiful lake.
Shinanomachi

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:06.660
That is Lake Nojiriko.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:11.710
It is an inviolable rule for Americans to have a lake at their summer resort.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:17.670
It seems that they find it hard to understand why
Karuizawa is more popular with the Japanese.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:21.590
So, there are so many foreigners here

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.720
that Shinanomachi is considered
the “foreigners’ Karuizawa,” right?

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.760
Oh, I’m surprised that you know that.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.010
I’ve done basic research on the place, you know...

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.520
There are various specialty products in Shinanomachi, but...

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.940
If we’re going to make jam, then it must be rhubarb, right?

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.940
Even I was thinking of using rhubarb as an ingredient.

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:40.570
In Japan, it has been famous as an herbal
medicine, right since ancient times, right?

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:43.070
The word for it in Japanese is
“Daiou,” written as “Big” and “Yellow.”

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.070
That’s right!

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.610
What’s the matter with you?

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.830
Well, we can’t have you becoming a yakuza, right?

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.200
I looked it up with everything I had.

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:53.460
Kawachi-san...

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.620
Somehow you look kinda dependable this time around.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.880
What’s wrong, Azuma-kun?!

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:05.720
I’m just a little dizzy.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:06.890
It’s all right.

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:09.140
In that case, it’s all right...

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.180
We already know that our opponent is strong.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:15.390
If Azuma-kun was to collapse and was unable to participate, I’d have to fight all by myself.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.350
That’s right!

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:19.650
After all, I don’t figure into the equation at all.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.030
How mean to say that after just saying that I seem dependable.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.150
I was kidding. Just kidding.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.990
I was a little serious too, though.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:27.490
Well, anyway...

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.120
Since Azuma-kun doesn’t seem too well today either,

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:30.950
let’s go to the lodge and...

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.450
A-Azuma!

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.910
Azuma-kun!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.970
Acute tonsillitis, huh?

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.640
He’s got a high fever,

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.230
but I think he should be fine in three or four days.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.230
Take care.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.480
Well, I’m glad that it wasn’t anything serious, but...

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:04.940
Looks like this time we can’t really expect much of Azuma.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:07.360
Can’t be helped.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.730
For now, let’s acquire our main ingredient, rhubarb, as soon as possible.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:11.490
That’s right.

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:18.280
Looks like this might be my final match...

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.250
<b>Hashiguchi</b>

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.630
Hashiguchi Takashi
The third-generation head of the Hashiguchi Family

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:32.140
You think that it shouldn’t be allowed, Aoyagi?
Hashiguchi Takashi
The third-generation head of the Hashiguchi Family

00:14:32.140 --> 00:14:32.920
You think that it shouldn’t be allowed, Aoyagi?

00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:36.510
I think that choosing the fourth-generation head
of the Hashiguchi family through a cooking battle

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:38.550
really is taking it a little too far.

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:41.140
Don’t you think that there are more thug-like ways of determining...?

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:43.020
This is what Masanobu wished.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:46.100
He had never met Shigeru,

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.440
yet he grew up constantly hearing of his rumors.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:49.980
The Young Master Shigeru...

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:52.650
He’s only two, but they say he can already do factorization!

00:14:52.650 --> 00:14:54.030
What a genius.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:55.240
What a prodigy!

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:58.620
I think it’s hard for us to imagine this, but...

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:03.330
Masanobu probably ended up having a strong inferiority complex against Shigeru.

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:06.920
But even then, he hates to lose at anything.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:10.000
Leaving aside the problem of who inherits...

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:14.300
I think that he just wants to win at his specialization against Shigeru just once.

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:16.470
Is that so...?

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.590
While the subject matter is cooking,

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.850
there is no doubt that this is a battle with a man’s pride and spirit at stake.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:22.770
I see...

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:28.400
When I was young, I wanted to be a manga artist.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.320
I had my cute times too.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.230
Huh?
I had my cute times too.

00:15:32.230 --> 00:15:34.940
As a father, I don’t quite know what to think...

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:42.950
of forcing my sons, who have
discovered their own paths, into this world.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.700
Oh, this is rhubarb...?

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.000
Daiou, huh?

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:51.460
Is it really all right to turn this strange herb into jam?

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.300
How about taking a bite?

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.260
You want me to eat it raw?!

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:57.630
It’s pretty good.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:58.680
Here you go.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.860
What is this feeling?!

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:10.060
What are you doing, Kawachi-san?!

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:10.690
Ow–

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:13.190
All right!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:19.200
This sweet and sour taste is truly the sign
of the king of ingredients suitable for jam.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:20.620
Renamed as Daiou.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:20.950
Rhubarb = King
Renamed as Daiou.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.370
King. King. King. King. King.
Rhubarb = King

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:24.000
Kawachi-san...
That’s the wrong way of writing it.
Rhubarb = King

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.700
Rhubarb
Kawachi-san...
That’s the wrong way of writing it.
Rhubarb = King

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:25.710
Rhubarb = King
Rhubarb

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.750
We are satisfied.

00:16:29.750 --> 00:16:32.130
We shall bestow a crown upon thee as well.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.710
Oh, that was supposed to be a crown...

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:37.840
Now that Kanmuri is wearing a crown, this becomes a true crown.
Note: Kanmuri (<b>冠) means “crown.”</b>

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.680
And with this, we can win against any opponent.

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.180
What manner of strategy hast thou thought of?

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:43.890
“Thou”...?

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.350
Well, you see...

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.680
I believe that we must use freeze-concentration equipment.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.730
Freeze-concentration equipment, thou sayest?

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:51.190
Freeze-concentration equipment

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:53.960
It is a machine that can lower an item’s water content
Freeze-concentration equipment

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:54.610
by freezing at low temperatures under vacuum.
Freeze-concentration equipment

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:56.980
by freezing at low temperatures under vacuum.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.570
If you use it, mysteriously enough...

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:03.820
the food item can be processed
without losing its taste, fragrance or color,

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.450
leaving it as close to the original as possible.

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.080
Marvelous.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.910
This be a magic device thou speakest of, am I right?

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.500
As expected of a man of science,
what splendid knowledge.

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:15.210
In that case, Mr. Tsutsumi is no longer a threat.

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:17.670
No, with just that we couldn’t...

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.630
Looks like you’re having a lot of fun, Kanmuri-kun...

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:22.550
Tsutsumi-san!

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:25.260
He of humble birth hath appeared!

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:29.850
Should we get serious, someone like thyself would be finished in one fell swoop.

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:30.270
Come, come, come.

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:31.730
Please ignore that weird creature.
Come, come, come.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:32.900
Please ignore that weird creature.

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:34.020
Y... Yeah...

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:39.820
While it may have been coincidental, since I’ve heard your strategy, I’ll tell you mine as well.

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:43.870
While you’re using modern technology,

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:46.670
I plan to fight using the ultimate traditional technique.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:50.800
I plan to use the volcanic rocks present all around the vicinity.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.960
V-Volcanic rock...?

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.000
It can’t be that Tsutsumi-san plans on...?

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:01.050
My reaction wore off...

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:04.300
I’d like to have stayed in king
mode for a little while longer...

00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:06.050
Oh, what’s wrong Kanmuri...?

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.760
You look really serious.

00:18:07.760 --> 00:18:10.770
Tsutsumi-san plans on making jam fondue.

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:11.430
Huh?

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:12.520
Fondue?

00:18:13.020 --> 00:18:14.590
You mean like the cheese fondue stuff?

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:17.520
But, does that have anything to do with jam?

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:18.520
Very much so.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:24.500
By using volcanic rock as a pot, Tsutsumi-san plans on making the ultimate warm jam.

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.490
W-Warm jam...?

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:27.990
You don’t have any...?

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.710
Not here either, huh?

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:30.780
I see...

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:31.710
Thank you.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.750
Kanmuri... this is the tenth one.

00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:36.710
What the hell are you looking for?

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:39.720
Tsutsumi-san’s volcanic rock will
be a hard obstacle to overcome.

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:42.840
When you concentrate sticky substances like jam,

00:18:42.840 --> 00:18:45.090
they tend to immediately burn and stick to regular pots.

00:18:45.090 --> 00:18:46.760
But, with volcanic rock, that won’t happen.

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:49.350
When you boil it, strong far-infrared rays are emitted,

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.010
strongly bringing out the jam’s original flavor.

00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:53.400
That’s right.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:53.440
Far-infrared rays
That’s right.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:53.520
Far-infrared rays

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:58.520
In addition, jam is fundamentally
more delicious when warm.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:04.230
Have you ever eaten freshly made warm jam?

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:06.900
The high-class sweetness and flavor are enough to make your tongue melt.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:09.240
And the steam carries with it a refreshing fragrance.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:11.490
This is what true jam is.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:12.450
Yay.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.000
But!

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:13.540
<b>Jam
But!</b>

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:16.370
If you’re to just warm up jam that was
made by the freeze-concentration technique,
<b>Jam</b>

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:19.120
you lose the taste, the texture and the fragrance.
<b>Jam</b>

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:19.130
<b>Jam</b>

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:19.140
So, what is it that you need to overcome that problem?
<b>Jam</b>

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:22.960
So, what is it that you need to overcome that problem?

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:25.460
Tell me what you’re looking for already.

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:33.470
Hey you, what are you doing?!

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:35.560
I’m sorry!

00:19:35.560 --> 00:19:38.890
Well, thankfully nothing broke, but please be careful–

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:40.600
Huh?

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:42.020
I’m sorry!

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:43.360
Please show that to me!

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:46.110
This is it!

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:48.070
This is the wine that I was looking for!

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:48.870
Kifu wine!

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:51.160
This is called Nagano prefecture’s treasure.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.660
This is one of the highest-quality wines of Nagano.

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:54.740
What was that?!

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:57.330
Oh, is that what you guys were looking for?

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:58.380
You have good taste.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:01.080
I have an open bottle.

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.130
Would you like to try some?

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.170
Can we?!

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:04.170
That would be great!

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:07.390
But, I’m underaged, so would you do the honors, Kawachi-san?

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:09.450
I don’t quite get it,

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:13.150
but since it was the wine that Kanmuri was looking for, it must be really good.

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:15.810
Gifu!

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.320
Gifu!

00:20:19.060 --> 00:20:24.110
I know that it’s produced in Nagano, but
images of Gifu keep flowing into my head!

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:27.650
This is Kifu wine, huh?

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:29.740
This fragrance and this elegant sweetness...

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.700
This is unlike any wine I’ve ever had.

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.240
A truly first-rate wine.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:34.450
Right?

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:39.120
You probably had images from Gifu flow in because it’s right next to Nagano prefecture.

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:42.880
If we’re to mix this into jam,
we’ll be sure to make the ultimate jam.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:44.080
Yeah.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:45.790
With this, we might be able to beat him.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:47.630
Oh, just as expected of you, Kanmuri-kun.

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:51.060
That is a wonderful idea.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:52.300
Tsutsumi-san!

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:53.800
Why are you here?!

00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:56.060
Don’t worry.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:59.810
What I want is Nagano prefecture’s
specialty made from apples, the calvados.

00:20:59.810 --> 00:21:00.810
An apple brandy.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:03.030
Oh, I have some.

00:21:04.310 --> 00:21:06.360
Take care, everyone.

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:08.360
I wish you the very best.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:11.900
What’s with that carefree attitude of his?

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.070
We have to beat him into the ground.

00:21:14.070 --> 00:21:15.410
Right, Kanmuri?

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:16.410
No...

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:19.660
It’s probably us that are going to be beaten into the ground.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:23.170
He’s not trying to make jam fondue...

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:25.170
His true aim is a jam flambe.

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:29.890
He plans on making a Flaming Jam
that emits fire like a volcano.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:32.390
Azuma Kazuma

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:34.130
The patient is not here!

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:35.680
Oh no!

00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:38.480
Azuma Kazuma-san, the patient we
had admitted here, has disappeared!

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:40.810
Kusa Lodge
Note: Kusasou can also mean “Looks like it’ll stink” when written as <b>臭そう.</b>

00:21:40.810 --> 00:21:43.070
This is tonight’s lodge, Kusa Lodge.
Kusa Lodge

00:21:43.850 --> 00:21:45.070
Umm...

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:48.230
You’re surprised, right?

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:50.230
I picked a good lodge this time.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:53.070
This might be my last match, so...

00:21:53.070 --> 00:21:55.110
I splurged a little.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:21:59.950
I’m sorry, Kanmuri.

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:03.410
I really want to help you, but...

00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:06.550
I have neither the skill nor the ideas.

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:08.090
Kawachi-san...

00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:11.550
It’s all right. Don’t worry about me...

00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:16.510
I’m happy with just your feelings.

00:22:16.510 --> 00:22:17.770
You can’t do that.

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:19.770
You can’t do that, Kanmuri.

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:22.280
You mustn’t give up no matter what.

00:22:22.680 --> 00:22:23.280
Azuma-kun!
Azuma!

00:22:25.400 --> 00:22:27.480
No matter how strong the opponent is...

00:22:27.480 --> 00:22:29.520
if you don’t give up until the very end...

00:22:29.520 --> 00:22:32.400
there’s sure to be a way to win!

00:22:53.850 --> 00:23:02.150
The world will probably go on today, with a repetition of the same faces,

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:10.240
but there was one thing that I’d forgotten.

00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:14.970
If I’m to take a deep breath,

00:23:14.970 --> 00:23:19.000
then the shape of the love that permeates my surroundings

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:26.550
will shine so much that it’s blinding.

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:34.970
Someone is calling me from far away...

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:43.350
And that voice constantly echoes in my heart.

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:51.950
So, riding on my small pleasures, the merry-go-round begins to turn...

00:23:51.950 --> 00:24:02.460
And even on days when the morning doesn’t come, it shines a light in my heart.

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:06.980
Thank you, Azuma-kun.

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:08.340
I won’t give up no matter what.

00:24:08.340 --> 00:24:09.730
And I’ll cheer you on!

00:24:09.730 --> 00:24:10.400
It’s all thanks to you, Azuma-kun.
And I’ll cheer you on!

00:24:10.400 --> 00:24:10.680
It’s all thanks to you, Azuma-kun.

00:24:10.680 --> 00:24:11.820
But even I’m...

00:24:11.820 --> 00:24:13.150
Thank you, Azuma-kun!

